    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="0665" n="557" xml:id="pg557"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Sir Julian Pauncefote</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Personal.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic">May 20,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir Julian</hi>: The President is desirous to
                    learn the reply of Her Majesty’s Government to the proposition submitted in
                    Department’s note of the 4th instant, to stop sealing by citizens of the United
                    States as well as by subjects of Her Majesty, pending the arbitration of
                    questions in dispute touching the seal fisheries in Behring Sea.</p>
                <p>I should be glad to know as soon as possible the present state of the matter.</p>
                <p>I remain, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
